  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SECURING CHIMPANZEE CONSERVATION IN THE MAHALE TONGWE WEST CORRIDOR, TANZANIA #2. 2021 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CONTRIBUTE TO THE SURVIVAL OF ENDANGERED CHIMPANZEES IN TANZANIA S GREATER MAHALE ECOSYSTEM AND PROTECT A KEY HABITAT CORRIDOR BY: (1) EQUIPPING AND TRAINING VILLAGE FOREST SCOUTS INCLUDING THE PROVISION OF GPSS, CAMERAS, BINOCULARS, AND FOOTWEAR (2) INCREASING VILLAGE CAPACITY TO DERIVE A SUSTAINABLE INCOME FROM VILLAGE FORESTS BY AUGMENTING THE NUMBER OF COMMUNITY CONSERVATION BANK (COCOBA) MICRO-FINANCE SYSTEMS, DEVELOPING ALTERNATIVE LIVELIHOODS, IMPLEMENTING A CARBON CREDIT INCOME PROJECT, AND PROVIDING GOVERNANCE TRAINING (3) CONDUCTING BIODIVERSITY SURVEYS TO BETTER UNDERSTAND CORRIDOR USE BY CHIMPANZEES AND OTHER KEY SPECIES AND (4) CONDUCTING A SOCIO-ECONOMIC SURVEY TO UNDERSTAND DRIVERS OF HUMAN IN-MIGRATION AND ENCROACHMENT ON CHIMPANZEE HABITAT.</narrative>
  </description>
